---
// src/tools/media/image-converter/About.astro
import { AccordionCard } from '@/core/components/ui';
---

<AccordionCard title="How to use this tool" defaultOpen={true} client:load>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mt-2">
    <div class="flex gap-4">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">1</div>
      <div>
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mb-1">Upload an Image</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Drop a JPG, PNG, WebP, AVIF, JXL, BMP, GIF, ICO, TGA, TIFF, EPS, PSD, SVG, or HEIC file into the upload area.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex gap-4">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">2</div>
      <div>
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mb-1">Pick a Format</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Choose from 10 writable formats. EPS, PSD, and SVG are input-only and will be rasterized before conversion.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex gap-4">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">3</div>
      <div>
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm mb-1">Convert & Download</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm">Hit Convert. The worker handles decoding and encoding off the main thread. Download the result or send it to another tool.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</AccordionCard>

<AccordionCard title="Project Overview" client:load>
  <p class="mb-4">
    Image Converter transforms images between 10 writable formats entirely in your browser. EPS, PSD, and SVG inputs are supported for rasterization, while HEIC files from iPhones use a dedicated decode path.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every conversion runs inside a Web Worker using a unified pipeline of jSquash, image-in-browser, pscat, and resvg-wasm codecs. No uploads, no servers, no accounts.
  </p>
</AccordionCard>

<AccordionCard title="Under the hood (Architecture)" client:load>
  <p class="mb-4">
    This tool is built on a strict client-side pipeline:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 mb-4 text-sm">
    <li><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Codecs:</strong> jSquash for JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF, JXL. image-in-browser for BMP, GIF, ICO, TGA, TIFF, PSD. pscat for EPS. resvg-wasm for SVG.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">HEIC Input:</strong> heic2any decodes HEIC inside the worker before the jSquash pipeline runs.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Worker:</strong> All decoding and encoding happens off the main thread via a module worker.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Storage:</strong> File references live in the shared file store; raw bytes never leave the browser.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Zero backend. Zero API keys. Pure local computation.
  </p>
</AccordionCard>